findings.body:
The new assertion in `BlockedWebSocketCompressionTests` uses `&&` between the old and new CSP patterns. The browser emits one log line in one format or the other, so `logs[0].Message` can match at most one regex and the `&&` is always false. The assertion message already says "match one of", which contradicts the code.

::diff{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerExecutionTests/WebSocketCompressionTests.cs" lines="107-110"}

The intent is to accept either message format, so the operator should be `||`.

::suggestion{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerExecutionTests/WebSocketCompressionTests.cs" lines="107-110"}
Assert.True(
    ParseErrorMessageRegexOld.IsMatch(logs[0].Message) ||
    ParseErrorMessageRegexNew.IsMatch(logs[0].Message),
    $"Expected log message to match one of the CSP error patterns: {ParseErrorMessageRegexOld} or {ParseErrorMessageRegexNew}. Actual: {logs[0].Message}");

The `condition` default in the source-index stage1 template changes from empty (always run) to `eq(variables['Build.SourceBranch'], 'refs/heads/main')`. The template is reached through `eng/common/core-templates/jobs/jobs.yml`, so every caller that does not pass its own condition now skips source indexing on non-main branches. This PR targets `release/9.0`, so the source-index stage will stop running there with no error. This is a behavior change inside a dependency-bump PR, and the PR description doesn't mention it.

::diff{file="eng/common/core-templates/job/source-index-stage1.yml" lines="9-9"}

If this gating is intentional, it should come from the arcade source with a note. If it isn't, restore the empty default and let callers opt in.

The internal runtime source args now point at `https://ci.dot.net/internal` but still pass `$(dotnetbuilds-internal-container-read-token-base64)` as the feed key. The previous host was `dotnetbuilds.blob.core.windows.net/internal`, which is the blob container the token was issued for. I can't verify from this repo that `ci.dot.net` accepts the same credential. If it doesn't, internal source builds that set this token will fail to restore the runtime. The change also isn't tied to any dependency bump.

::diff{file="eng/common/core-templates/steps/source-build.yml" lines="44-44"}

Confirm with the arcade owners that the token is valid for the new host, and that `ci.dot.net/internal` is the intended endpoint for release/9.0.

The arcade bump is mixed with changes to `RedisEndToEnd.cs` that have nothing to do with it. Two tests get `[QuarantinedTest]` attributes, which means their failures are reported as expected instead of blocking CI. The first is issue 59991 on `CanSendAndReceiveUserMessagesFromMultipleConnectionsWithSameUser`, and the second is issue 63582 on `CanSendAndReceiveUserMessagesUserNameWithPatternIsTreatedAsLiteral`. Quarantines should be a deliberate, separately reviewed decision. Bundling them into a Maestro update hides the change from the people who review test health. The disposal order in the second test is also swapped.

::diff{file="src/SignalR/server/StackExchangeRedis/test/RedisEndToEnd.cs" lines="92-92"}

Split these into their own PR with a link to the tracking issue and an explanation of why each test is flaky.

`WebSocketWrapper.ReceiveAsync` now resets `_receiveTcs` before the zero-byte early return, not after the copy. Before this change, a zero-byte read left the already-completed TCS in place, so the next read returned the same result immediately. The new order fixes that, but it's a behavior change in test infrastructure that the PR doesn't explain. The `sealed` modifier on `WebSocketWrapper` was also dropped with no stated reason. Neither change is needed for the arcade bump.

::diff{file="src/SignalR/server/StackExchangeRedis/test/RedisEndToEnd.cs" lines="409-409"}

If the reset-order fix is wanted, call it out in the commit message and add a test for zero-byte reads. Restore `sealed` unless a subclass needs it.

The internal source-build pool image changes from `1es-mariner-2` to `1es-azurelinux-3`. Nothing in this repo confirms that the image exists in the `NetCore1ESPool-Internal` and `NetCore1ESPool-Svc-Internal` pools. If it doesn't, the job will fail to schedule rather than run a degraded build. This is a pipeline infrastructure change, so the check belongs with the arcade or infra owners.

::diff{file="eng/common/core-templates/job/source-build.yml" lines="68-68"}

Confirm the image name with the infrastructure team before merging.
